findings.finding:
The rule reads every store entry raw: it neither runs check_split nor verifies the key against the entry's digest, unlike every other reference in the model. Adding one same-suite entry under a key that is not its digest to the store of the valid selection V74 changes the result in four ways:
(N5a) an entry whose partitions is a list gives SHAPE;
(N5e) an unhashable task digest gives SHAPE;
(N5b) an entry that is not a declaration at all (wrong schemaVersion) still holds tasks out and gives HELD_OUT_SELECTION;
(N5d) a PARTITION_EMPTY declaration does the same.
These are fail-closed, not false accepts, but two consumers with differently curated stores reach different results for the same selection. Separately, the rule ignores time: a valid declaration dated after every run that holds out a task used in development retroactively refuses the selection (N5c).
